            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0172" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1415: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-28T14:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1940—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2331. Embassy, Vichy, requested repeat to you its 413, August 23, noon, and 430,
                    August 26, 1 p.m.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d216-f1"/> Upon receipt please request
                    German Foreign Office urgently to consider the situation of Americans in France
                    desiring to return to United States, who are being prevented from doing so by
                    delay in obtaining exit visas from German authorities and restrictions on
                    exportation of currency. With respect to latter restrictions, as it appears to
                    be impossible for Americans in France to purchase through transportation there
                    to United States, they should at least be allowed to depart with sufficient
                    dollars or other currency to enable them to proceed through Spain and Portugal
                    and purchase transportation to New York from Lisbon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
